1
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:42,260
Settling things like hazardous chemicals or specimens requires a great deal of caution.
处理危险化学品或样本之类的东西，需要格外谨慎。

2
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:47,540
If we don't contain them, hazards can spread and contaminate the things around them, including
如果我们不把它们控制住，危害就会扩散，污染周围的东西，包括

3
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:51,980
you and your co-workers.
你和你的同事。

4
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:57,760
Every day we're called on to handle substances like toxins, corrosives, and carcinogens.
我们每天都要处理毒物、腐蚀性物质和致癌物之类的物质。

5
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:03,480
We think we know how to protect ourselves, but are we doing all we can?
我们以为自己知道如何保护自己，但我们真的做到了一切能做的吗？

6
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:08,280
Having tiny amounts of a hazardous material combined with a few unconscious actions can
极少量的危险物质，再加上几个无意识的动作，就可能

7
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:10,560
spread contamination.
使污染扩散。

8
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:14,600
Let's take a closer look.
我们来仔细看一看。

9
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:19,200
The luminescent dye that's been added to this material makes it easy to trace the path of
这种物质中加入了荧光染料，便于追踪

10
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,000
any contamination.
任何污染的路径。

11
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,120
As we can see, the dye has been spread from the liquid on the outside of the test tube
我们可以看到，染料从试管外壁的液体上

12
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:42,240
to the lab worker themself, and can then be transferred to everything they touch.
扩散到了实验人员身上，然后又会被转移到他们碰到的所有东西上。

13
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:47,520
When it's this easy for contamination to occur, we need to do everything we can to prevent
既然污染这么容易发生，我们就需要尽一切努力去防止

14
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:48,520
it.
它。

15
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:55,660
This means being very careful with the products we work with and how we handle them.
这意味着要非常小心我们所使用的产品以及我们处理它们的方式。

16
00:01:55,660 --> 00:02:00,900
To effectively shield ourselves from contamination, we need to first know about the materials we're
要有效地保护自己免受污染，我们首先需要了解我们

17
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,540
working with.
所使用的物质。

18
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:10,170
So you need to read product labels and safety data sheets before starting to use a substance.
所以在开始使用一种物质之前，你需要阅读产品标签和安全技术说明书。

19
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:14,850
These and other references describe the potential hazards presented by the material, and they
这些以及其他参考资料描述了该物质可能带来的危害，还

20
00:02:14,850 --> 00:02:20,620
tell us how to protect ourselves from contamination.
告诉我们如何保护自己免受污染。

21
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:25,480
As we think about protecting ourselves, we need to consider the four major roots of
在考虑如何保护自己时，我们需要考虑物质进入人体的四种主要

22
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:33,000
entry a material has to our bodies – inhalation, eye contact, skin contact, absorption and
途径——吸入、眼睛接触、皮肤接触、吸收和

23
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,880
injection, and ingestion.
注射，以及食入。

24
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:43,120
We can guard these roots of entry by using a combination of personal protective equipment
我们可以结合使用个人防护装备

25
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:48,480
PPE, engineering controls, and safe work practices.
PPE、工程控制和安全作业规范来守住这些进入途径。

26
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:53,390
Let's start with personal protective equipment.
我们先从个人防护装备说起。

27
00:02:53,390 --> 00:02:57,470
It needs to be inspected before you put it on.
在穿戴之前需要对它进行检查。

28
00:02:57,470 --> 00:03:01,870
Replace any items that are ripped or otherwise damaged, and make sure you've got a proper
更换任何撕破或有其他损坏的物品，并确保尺寸

29
00:03:01,870 --> 00:03:04,390
fit.
合身。

30
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:10,190
At a minimum, you should wear gloves, a lab coat, and safety eyewear.
至少你应该戴手套、穿实验服、戴安全护目镜。

31
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:13,310
Some operations demand even more protection.
有些操作还要求更多的防护。

32
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:17,210
For instance, face shields should be worn if there's a danger of chemical splashes
例如，如果有化学品溅到头部、面部和颈部的危险，

33
00:03:17,210 --> 00:03:21,350
to the head, face, and neck area.
就应该戴面罩。

34
00:03:21,350 --> 00:03:26,270
You need to anticipate the hazards associated with the materials you're working with,
你需要预见到与你所用物质相关的危害，

35
00:03:26,270 --> 00:03:30,950
and talk to your supervisor to make sure that you're using all the PPE that you need
并和你的主管沟通，确保你使用了所有需要的个人防护装备，

36
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:34,650
to be fully protected.
从而得到充分保护。

37
00:03:34,650 --> 00:03:38,710
You should also monitor the condition of your protective equipment throughout the day,
你还应该在一天中随时留意防护装备的状况，

38
00:03:38,710 --> 00:03:45,660
and immediately replace anything that's damaged or that may have become contaminated.
一旦有任何东西损坏或可能已被污染，立即更换。

39
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,940
Pay special attention to your gloves.
要特别注意你的手套。

40
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:52,540
Perspiration on the inside and other liquids on the outside can make gloves permeable
手套内侧的汗液和外侧的其他液体，会使手套变得可渗透，

41
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:58,340
to the very thing you're trying to prevent – contamination.
恰恰让你想要防止的东西——污染——透过来。

42
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:04,840
Change your gloves at least once every two hours, or as soon as they become wet.
至少每两小时更换一次手套，或者手套一湿就立即更换。

43
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:10,020
You should also look at how you can use engineering controls to protect against contamination
你还应该考虑如何利用工程控制来防止污染，

44
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:14,930
when you're working with hazardous materials.
在你处理危险物质的时候。

45
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:19,190
Equipment like splash guards and blast shields can protect your skin and eyes from inadvertent
防溅挡板和防爆护罩之类的设备，可以保护你的皮肤和眼睛，避免意外

46
00:04:19,190 --> 00:04:22,710
chemical contact.
接触化学品。

47
00:04:22,710 --> 00:04:26,650
Exhaust hoods and other ventilation devices will keep contaminated fumes and vapors out
排风罩和其他通风装置能让受污染的烟气和蒸气远离

48
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:29,490
of your breathing zone.
你的呼吸区。

49
00:04:29,490 --> 00:04:33,390
Consult your supervisor about the engineering controls you can use in your lab to limit
向你的主管咨询，在你的实验室里可以使用哪些工程控制来限制

50
00:04:33,390 --> 00:04:46,400
the spread of contamination.
污染的扩散。

51
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:51,680
Even with the proper PPE and engineering controls, contamination can still occur if
即使有合适的个人防护装备和工程控制，如果

52
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:55,120
you don't follow safe work practices.
你不遵守安全作业规范，污染仍然可能发生。

53
00:04:55,120 --> 00:05:01,150
To start, this means paying attention to good housekeeping.
首先，这意味着要注意保持良好的内务整洁。

54
00:05:01,150 --> 00:05:03,650
Keep your work area neat and orderly.
让你的工作区域整齐有序，

55
00:05:03,650 --> 00:05:05,450
Avoid unnecessary clutter.
避免不必要的杂乱。

56
00:05:05,450 --> 00:05:09,930
Wherever possible, use small containers.
只要有可能，就使用小容器。

57
00:05:09,930 --> 00:05:15,110
And if you're not using a substance, put it back where it belongs.
如果你不用某种物质了，就把它放回原处。

58
00:05:15,110 --> 00:05:18,930
Any spill should be cleaned up as quickly as possible.
任何溅洒都应尽快清理干净。

59
00:05:18,930 --> 00:05:25,980
Follow proper disposal procedures and decontaminate the spill area.
遵守正确的处置程序，并对溅洒区域进行去污。

60
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:30,380
When you're finished with a piece of equipment, make sure that it's cleaned up and decontaminated
用完一件设备后，要确保把它清理干净并去污，

61
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:32,460
before you leave for the day.
然后再下班离开。

62
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:36,640
You don't know who might need to use it later.
你不知道之后谁可能需要用它。

63
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:40,880
If you can't clean glassware immediately, soak it in soap and water.
如果你不能立即清洗玻璃仪器，就把它浸泡在肥皂水中。

64
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:47,140
This will cut down on contamination and make cleanup easier.
这样可以减少污染，也让清洗更容易。

65
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:53,060
You should plan for the disposal of hazardous or infectious waste before you begin a procedure.
在开始一项操作之前，你就应该计划好危险废物或感染性废物的处置。

66
00:05:53,060 --> 00:06:00,120
Your lab has a written policy on handling this type of waste, so follow it.
你的实验室有处理这类废物的书面规定，所以要遵照执行。

67
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:02,320
Be careful what you pour down the drain.
小心你往下水道里倒的东西。

68
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:06,040
The sewer system is not built to handle laboratory chemicals.
排水系统并不是为处理实验室化学品而建的。

69
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:10,840
A mistake in disposal could contaminate the local supply of drinking water and other parts
处置上的失误可能会污染当地的饮用水供应以及环境中的

70
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:13,560
of the environment.
其他部分。

71
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:29,080
Ask your supervisor or safety officer about your lab's disposal procedures.
向你的主管或安全员询问你们实验室的处置程序。

72
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:33,840
Another problem with contamination is its potential for personal transportation.
污染的另一个问题是，它可能会被人随身带走。

73
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:37,840
When you're on a break, off to lunch, or on your way home, it can be easy to take a
当你休息、去吃午饭或者下班回家时，很容易把

74
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:41,320
contaminant with you.
污染物随身带走。

75
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:44,760
Leave notebooks, pencils, and other supplies in the lab.
把笔记本、铅笔和其他用品留在实验室里。

76
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:49,640
Anything you use in your work should be thought of as being contaminated.
你工作中用到的任何东西都应被视为已受污染。

77
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:54,880
Wash your hands thoroughly before leaving your work area.
离开工作区域前要彻底洗手。

78
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:58,440
Never wear your PPE or lab coat outside the lab.
绝不要穿戴个人防护装备或实验服走出实验室。

79
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:02,120
That can cause real problems.
那会造成真正的问题。

80
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:06,800
For instance, gloves can leave contaminants on doorknobs, which in turn can contaminate
例如，手套会把污染物留在门把手上，进而又会污染

81
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:12,080
the next person coming through the door.
下一个进门的人。

82
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:17,120
Poor safety practices can also increase the risk of ingesting hazardous materials.
不良的安全习惯还会增加食入危险物质的风险。

83
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:21,160
Something as simple as taking your lab notebook to lunch could lead to contaminating your
像把实验记录本带去吃午饭这样简单的事情，就可能导致你的

84
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:24,140
sandwich.
三明治受到污染。

85
00:07:24,140 --> 00:07:28,060
Of course, this type of problem can also occur inside the lab.
当然，这类问题在实验室里面也可能发生。

86
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:31,580
Never bring food or drink into your lab area.
绝不要把食物或饮料带进实验室区域。

87
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:36,740
Don't wash your coffee cup or lunch dishes in the lab sink.
不要在实验室水槽里清洗你的咖啡杯或午餐餐具。

88
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:42,460
The rule of thumb for avoiding ingestion hazards is never mix contaminants with uncontaminated
避免食入危害的经验法则是：绝不要让污染物与未受污染的

89
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:45,500
objects or areas.
物品或区域混在一起。

90
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:49,500
You also need to remember that contaminants move easily from one part of your body to
你还要记住，污染物很容易从身体的一个部位转移到

91
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:50,860
another.
另一个部位。

92
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:55,100
So you should avoid nervous habits like rubbing your face or scratching your nose.
所以你应该避免揉脸或挠鼻子之类的紧张小动作，

93
00:07:55,100 --> 00:08:08,930
They can bring hazards too close to your mouth.
它们会把危害带到离你嘴巴太近的地方。

94
00:08:08,930 --> 00:08:14,630
It's also important to protect the materials that you're working with from contamination.
保护你所使用的材料免受污染也很重要。

95
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:18,970
It's all too easy to contaminate a sample with a chemical unknown that can result in
样品很容易被某种未知化学物质污染，从而导致

96
00:08:18,970 --> 00:08:21,370
a false reading.
错误的读数。

97
00:08:21,370 --> 00:08:25,750
To prevent the contamination of samples and other materials, keep your work surfaces and
为防止样品和其他材料受到污染，要保持你的工作台面和

98
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:27,250
equipment clean.
设备清洁。

99
00:08:27,250 --> 00:08:33,720
Check them before, during, and after your work.
在工作之前、期间和之后都要检查它们。

100
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:36,680
Decontaminate all the equipment after using it.
使用后对所有设备进行去污。

101
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:37,680
Be thorough.
要彻底。

102
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:43,810
Follow your lab's established cleaning procedures.
遵守你们实验室既定的清洁程序。

103
00:08:43,810 --> 00:08:47,650
Pay special attention to equipment that's shared with other workers.
要特别注意与其他人员共用的设备。

104
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:52,490
Hot plates and stirrers, for example, tend to collect chemical residues over time.
比如加热板和搅拌器，时间一长往往会积聚化学残留物。

105
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:59,090
These residues can then contaminate the work that you're doing.
这些残留物进而会污染你正在做的工作。

106
00:08:59,090 --> 00:09:04,370
When cleaning equipment or your lab area, make sure to use appropriate cleaning methods.
清洁设备或实验室区域时，一定要使用合适的清洁方法。

107
00:09:04,370 --> 00:09:06,650
Don't use air guns to blow away powder.
不要用气枪吹走粉末，

108
00:09:06,650 --> 00:09:12,050
It could easily contaminate other areas and employees.
那很容易污染其他区域和人员。

109
00:09:12,050 --> 00:09:21,840
Simply blot or sweep up the powder with a dry paper towel and dispose of it properly.
只需用干纸巾把粉末吸干或扫起来，并妥善处置。

110
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:28,160
Keeping things free from contamination is critical to safe and productive lab operations.
使物品免受污染，对于实验室安全而高效地运行至关重要。

111
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:30,940
Let's review.
我们来回顾一下。

112
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:33,320
Know what materials you're dealing with.
了解你所处理的是什么物质，

113
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:36,520
Don't make assumptions.
不要想当然。

114
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:41,880
Wear PPE and dispose of it properly when you're finished.
穿戴个人防护装备，用完后妥善处置。

115
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:46,960
Use the correct engineering controls for the work that you're doing.
针对你所做的工作使用正确的工程控制。

116
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:51,520
Maintain good housekeeping practices.
保持良好的内务整洁习惯，

117
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:52,840
And work carefully.
并且小心操作。

118
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:58,640
Be aware of the substances and equipment you come into contact with.
留意你接触到的物质和设备。

119
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:03,560
Most importantly, remember that the best way to prevent contamination is to be mindful of
最重要的是，记住防止污染的最好方法，是心里想着

120
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:08,600
those who worked before you and considerate of those who will work after you.
在你之前工作过的人，并替在你之后工作的人着想。
